<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alonso de León</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1639–1691</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alonso de León (c. 1639–1691) was a Spanish soldier and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coahuila">Coahuila</a> who led several expeditions into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> in search of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rene-robert-cavelier-sieur-de-la-salle">La Salle</a>'s French colony. In 1689 he found the ruins of Fort Saint Louis on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matagorda-bay">Matagorda Bay</a>, and in 1690 he escorted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franciscans">Franciscans</a> to east Texas, where they founded the mission of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a> de los Tejas among the Hasinai.</p></div>
